  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "The total in-store price for an appliance is \\(\\$99.99.\\) A television commercial advertises the same product for three easy payments of \\(\\$29.98\\) and a one-time shipping and handling charge of \\(\\$9.98.\\) How much is saved by buying the appliance from the television advertiser?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(6\\) cents",
    "B": "\\(7\\) cents",
    "C": "\\(8\\) cents",
    "D": "\\(9\\) cents",
    "E": "\\(10\\) cents"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The advertised cost includes all three payments and the shipping charge once. Its total, in dollars, is\n\\[\n3(29.98)+9.98\n=89.94+9.98\n=99.92.\n\\]\nSubtracting this from the in-store price gives the saving:\n\\[\n99.99-99.92=0.07.\n\\]\nTherefore the saving is \\(\\boxed{7\\text{ cents}}\\), choice \\(\\text{B}\\).",
